Source: lucid-tokens
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Javid Medina <javidamedina@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/LucidOS-Project/lucid-tokens
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: lucid-tokens
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: the LucidOS configuration model, and its command line
 A layered resolver for desktop settings. A value stops being a magic number
 inside one program and becomes a setting the whole desktop can see, document,
 validate, revert and say where it came from.
 .
 Three layers, resolved in order: the compiled-in defaults, the distribution's
 opinions in /usr/share/lucid/profile.d, and the user's in
 ~/.config/lucid/profile.d. Every key declares a default and bounds, and values
 outside them are clamped rather than trusted. Every layer's value is kept
 rather than only the winning one, so undoing a user's change falls back to the
 distribution's rather than past it.
 .
 This package carries the lucid-tokens command, which lists, sets, resets and
 explains keys -- including which layer a value came from.

Package: liblucid-tokens-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: the LucidOS configuration model -- header and static library
 Development files for lucid-tokens.
 .
 A static library rather than a shared object, deliberately, while the
 interface is still moving: a .so is a promise about an ABI, and making that
 promise before the API has settled is worse than not making it.
 .
 It exists so that lucid-bar and lucid-panel can build against this rather than
 vendoring the source, which is what they did before -- and which meant a
 changed default required every consumer to be rebuilt and re-uploaded.
